The answer is a labelled diagram of the **water cycle**, drawn by the candidate. A full-mark diagram shows:

- the **sun** supplying the heat;
- **evaporation** (arrows going up) from the sea, lakes and rivers;
- **transpiration** (arrows going up) from the leaves of plants, and water vapour given off by animals (respiration, sweating);
- **condensation** of the water vapour to form **clouds**;
- **precipitation** (rain, hail, snow) falling on the land and the sea;
- **surface run-off** to streams, rivers and the sea;
- **infiltration** into the soil to form **ground water**, with **absorption** of water by the roots of plants (and drinking by animals);
- arrows showing the direction of each process, and a title (*The water cycle*).
